    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0543" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.00/7–1844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of Strategic Services</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Donovan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-18">18 July, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am enclosing herewith
                    copy of two dispatches received from the Bern office of this agency,<anchor
                        n="46" xml:id="d301-f1"/> which I feel will be of interest to you. These
                    dispatches form a sequel to a report dated 16 May 1944 (forwarded to you on 17
                    May) concerning an opposition group in Germany, including some high military
                    figures, which favors peace.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> J. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Donovan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d301-a1.xml" xpointer="d301-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d301-f1" n="46" xml:id="d301-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably the two despatches here referred to were combined into the one
                    document enclosed, below. No other enclosure was found in the Department
                    files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
